 "title": "Permutation in String",
 "slug": "permutation-in-string",
 "category": "sliding-window",
 "difficulty": "Medium",
 "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/permutation-in-string/",
 "pattern": "Fixed-size sliding window + letter counts",
 "statement": "Given strings `s1` and `s2`, return `True` if some **substring of `s2`** is a permutation of `s1` — that is, it uses exactly the same letters, in any order.",
 "example": {
  "input": "s1 = \"ab\", s2 = \"eidbaooo\"",
  "output": "True",
  "why": "The substring \"ba\" of s2 is a rearrangement of \"ab\"."
 },
 "more": [
  {
   "input": "s1 = \"ab\", s2 = \"eidboaoo\"",
   "output": "False"
  },
  {
   "input": "s1 = \"adc\", s2 = \"dcda\"",
   "output": "True"
  },
  {
   "input": "s1 = \"abc\", s2 = \"ab\"",
   "output": "False"
  }
 ],
 "idea": [
  "A permutation of `s1` has the same length and exactly the same letter counts as `s1`.",
  "So slide a window of length `len(s1)` across `s2` and compare its letter counts with those of `s1`.",
  "Do not recount each window from scratch: when the window slides one step, one letter enters on the right and one leaves on the left — update just those two counts."
 ],
 "code": "class Solution:\n    def checkInclusion(self, s1: str, s2: str) -> bool:\n        if len(s1) > len(s2):\n            return False\n\n        char_freq_s1 = {}\n        for char in s1:\n            char_freq_s1[char] = char_freq_s1.get(char, 0) + 1\n\n        left, right = 0, 0\n        char_freq_temp = {}\n\n        while right < len(s2):\n            char_freq_temp[s2[right]] = char_freq_temp.get(s2[right], 0) + 1\n\n            if right - left + 1 == len(s1):\n                if char_freq_temp == char_freq_s1:\n                    return True\n                char_freq_temp[s2[left]] -= 1\n                if char_freq_temp[s2[left]] == 0:\n                    del char_freq_temp[s2[left]]\n                left += 1\n\n            right += 1\n\n        return False",
 "complexity": {
  "time": "O(n)",
  "timeWhy": "Each character of `s2` enters and leaves the window once; comparing two maps of at most 26 letters is O(1).",
  "space": "O(1)",
  "spaceWhy": "Two count maps with at most 26 entries each."
 },
